        <abstract>
            <para>The Oregon Bee Atlas is an initiative to characterize the wild bees and their floral relations in Oregon. Fieldwork is conducted primarily by Oregon State University Extension Service volunteer Master Melittologists.

This dataset aggregates previously published data from 2018, and 2019, and will be the sole source of occurrence records for the program with updates and additions provided annually.

For data inquiries contact lincoln.best&amp;#64;oregonstate.edu .</para>
        </abstract>
